# "{T}, Sacrifice this creature: Choose an exiled card an opponent owns with a void counter on it. You may play it this
# turn without paying its mana cost." Bot2 discards Lightning Bolt and a Mountain to Faithless Looting under Bot1's
# Dauthi Voidwalker, so both are exiled with a void counter instead (CR 614.1), and so is Faithless Looting as it
# leaves the stack. Bot1 sacrifices Dauthi Voidwalker, chooses among the three, and casts the Bolt from Bot2's exile
# with no mana. Dauthi Voidwalker is gone by then, so the Bolt goes to its owner's graveyard when it resolves, and the
# other two stay in exile with their void counters.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Dauthi Voidwalker
Swamp x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Faithless Looting
Mountain x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dauthi Voidwalker.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Faithless Looting.Cast
Bot2.Choose(Lightning Bolt; Mountain)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Dauthi Voidwalker.Activate
Bot1.Choose(Tap Dauthi Voidwalker)
Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Exile.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 5
Stack.Count = 0
Bot2.Life = 17
Exile = Faithless Looting; Mountain
Bot1.Graveyard = Dauthi Voidwalker
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
